{"type":"message","id":"4094e6a7","parentId":"12602621","timestamp":"2026-02-01T04:04:09.757Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_011g5bZVK4XgQtdMxfoNUABf","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- **Status:** Doug walking through daily workflows NEXT WEEK\n- **Next:** Detailed automation plan after walkthrough\n\n### 6. BluePrint Skill (General) ✅ OPERATIONAL\n- **What:** Chat-based construction doc intelligence tool\n- **Status:** Fully built and tested on USPS Greenwich CT (41 sheets, 559 spec pages, 11 rooms, Q&A 10/10)\n- **Pipeline:** Pass 1 (page-by-page) → Pass 2 (room-by-room synthesis) → Q&A\n- **Key rules:** Flag don't assume, room is atomic unit, partitions shared with two faces\n- **Location:** skills/blueprint/\n\n### 7. Bureh Dashboard ✅ RUNNING\n- **Stack:** React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind\n- **Features:** Overview, Memory, Projects, Investments, Cost Tracker, System Health\n- **Status:** Running on PM2, cost tracker live, dynamic projects\n- **Location:** projects/bureh-dashboard/\n\n### 8. Haven (Home Maintenance Tech) 💤 DORMANT\n- **What:** AI-first concierge home repair/maintenance\n- **Status:** Sector report complete. No active development.\n- **TAM:** $90-210B+, no competitor has AI as core intelligence layer\n\n## Strategic Priorities (confirmed Jan 30)\n1. JOC Translator — revival, landing page, demo, test with 5 contacts\n2. MedTech Bot concept note — DONE ✅\n3. 10x PM Automation — Doug walkthrough next week\n4. Global health consulting positioning\n5. Investment monitoring\n\n## Infrastructure & Config\n- **Server:** AWS EC2 (Amazon Linux 2023)\n- **API keys:** Anthropic (Claude Opus 4.5), Brave Search (Free plan — 2K queries/month, rate limited)\n- **Kimi/Moonshot:** SUSPENDED — balance ran out, needs recharge or removal\n- **Email:** baibureh01@gmail.com / Casper99! (needs App Password for IMAP)\n- **ngrok:** Configured (authtoken on file) — unreliable, drops frequently\n- **Security:** DM policy locked to @Sahr_Lebbie, directory permissions 700, log redaction enabled\n\n## Key Lessons\n- Kimi K2.5 balance ran out and got stuck — need better model failover handling\n- ngrok tunnels unreliable — PM2 helps but not bulletproof\n- Job board deep links go stale fast — always verify before sharing\n- Doug wants a Mac Mini eventually for persistent browser automation\n- Multi-agent adversarial architecture > single smarter model (arxiv 2601.14351)\n- \"Reliability comes from organizational structure, not perfect components\"\n- Remote execution pattern: agents write code, only summaries return to context — keeps windows clean\n\n## Polymarket Notes\n- Doug interested, preliminary analysis done\n- Fed Chair market analyzed ($280M volume) — Rieder vs Warsh vs Waller\n- Strategy: edge-finding through research speed, Kelly Criterion sizing\n- Realistic: $100/day from $500 is gambling-tier, need bankroll first"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":28,"aggregated":"- **Status:** Doug walking through daily workflows NEXT WEEK\n- **Next:** Detailed automation plan after walkthrough\n\n### 6. BluePrint Skill (General) ✅ OPERATIONAL\n- **What:** Chat-based construction doc intelligence tool\n- **Status:** Fully built and tested on USPS Greenwich CT (41 sheets, 559 spec pages, 11 rooms, Q&A 10/10)\n- **Pipeline:** Pass 1 (page-by-page) → Pass 2 (room-by-room synthesis) → Q&A\n- **Key rules:** Flag don't assume, room is atomic unit, partitions shared with two faces\n- **Location:** skills/blueprint/\n\n### 7. Bureh Dashboard ✅ RUNNING\n- **Stack:** React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind\n- **Features:** Overview, Memory, Projects, Investments, Cost Tracker, System Health\n- **Status:** Running on PM2, cost tracker live, dynamic projects\n- **Location:** projects/bureh-dashboard/\n\n### 8. Haven (Home Maintenance Tech) 💤 DORMANT\n- **What:** AI-first concierge home repair/maintenance\n- **Status:** Sector report complete. No active development.\n- **TAM:** $90-210B+, no competitor has AI as core intelligence layer\n\n## Strategic Priorities (confirmed Jan 30)\n1. JOC Translator — revival, landing page, demo, test with 5 contacts\n2. MedTech Bot concept note — DONE ✅\n3. 10x PM Automation — Doug walkthrough next week\n4. Global health consulting positioning\n5. Investment monitoring\n\n## Infrastructure & Config\n- **Server:** AWS EC2 (Amazon Linux 2023)\n- **API keys:** Anthropic (Claude Opus 4.5), Brave Search (Free plan — 2K queries/month, rate limited)\n- **Kimi/Moonshot:** SUSPENDED — balance ran out, needs recharge or removal\n- **Email:** baibureh01@gmail.com / Casper99! (needs App Password for IMAP)\n- **ngrok:** Configured (authtoken on file) — unreliable, drops frequently\n- **Security:** DM policy locked to @Sahr_Lebbie, directory permissions 700, log redaction enabled\n\n## Key Lessons\n- Kimi K2.5 balance ran out and got stuck — need better model failover handling\n- ngrok tunnels unreliable — PM2 helps but not bulletproof\n- Job board deep links go stale fast — always verify before sharing\n- Doug wants a Mac Mini eventually for persistent browser automation\n- Multi-agent adversarial architecture > single smarter model (arxiv 2601.14351)\n- \"Reliability comes from organizational structure, not perfect components\"\n- Remote execution pattern: agents write code, only summaries return to context — keeps windows clean\n\n## Polymarket Notes\n- Doug interested, preliminary analysis done\n- Fed Chair market analyzed ($280M volume) — Rieder vs Warsh vs Waller\n- Strategy: edge-finding through research speed, Kelly Criterion sizing\n- Realistic: $100/day from $500 is gambling-tier, need bankroll first","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1769918649747}}
