{"type":"message","id":"fe723155","parentId":"79ea6ef7","timestamp":"2026-02-01T04:06:39.380Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_013G7MAMetwHj3yQW4Vu4BQB","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/scripts/STANDUP-CRON.md","content":"# Daily Standup Cron Setup\n\n## Schedule\n\n**7:00 AM ET = 12:00 UTC** (11:00 UTC during EDT, 12:00 during EST)\n\n## Option 1: Cron Job (Direct)\n\n```bash\n# Edit crontab\ncrontab -e\n\n# Add this line (12:00 UTC = 7:00 AM EST / 8:00 AM EDT)\n0 12 * * * /home/ec2-user/clawd/scripts/daily-standup.sh > /home/ec2-user/clawd/logs/standup-$(date +\\%Y-\\%m-\\%d).log 2>&1\n```\n\n## Option 2: Clawdbot Cron (Preferred)\n\nUse Clawdbot's built-in cron to fire to the main session (Bai Bureh), who formats and sends to Doug on Telegram:\n\n```\nSchedule: 0 12 * * * (daily at 12:00 UTC)\nTask: Run /home/ec2-user/clawd/scripts/daily-standup.sh, format the output as a Telegram message, and send to Doug.\n```\n\nThis way Bai Bureh can add commentary, check for urgent items, and personalize the briefing.\n\n## Option 3: PM2 Cron\n\n```bash\npm2 start /home/ec2-user/clawd/scripts/daily-standup.sh --name \"daily-standup\" --cron \"0 12 * * *\" --no-autorestart\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n```bash\n# Run manually to verify output\nbash /home/ec2-user/clawd/scripts/daily-standup.sh\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Script outputs to stdout — pipe to log file or let Clawdbot consume it\n- EDT vs EST: adjust by 1 hour seasonally, or use `TZ=America/New_York` in cron\n- For EDT-aware scheduling: `0 11 * * * TZ=America/New_York ...` (if your cron supports TZ)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":590,"cacheRead":29938,"cacheWrite":86,"totalTokens":30615,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.014750000000000001,"cacheRead":0.014969,"cacheWrite":0.0005375,"total":0.0302615}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1769918787721}}
